 work far below recomputing the ordering from scratch?\"\n },\n {\n  \"name\": \"dynamic_scc\",\n  \"tier\": \"core\",\n  \"title\": \"Dynamic strongly connected components\",\n  \"directed\": true,\n  \"update_mode\": \"mixed\",\n  \"question\": \"can the SCC partition of a directed graph be maintained under edge insertions and deletions, with per-update work far below recomputing the whole decomposition?\"\n },\n {\n  \"name\": \"reachability\",\n  \"tier\": \"core\",\n  \"title\": \"Dynamic single-source reachability\",\n  \"directed\": true,\n  \"update_mode\": \"mixed\",\n  \"question\": \"can the set of vertices reachable from a fixed source be maintained under edge insertions and deletions, cheaper than re-running the search after every update?\"\n },\n {\n  \"name\": \"dynamic_lbfs\",\n  \"tier\": \"open\",\n  \"title\": \"Dynamic lexicographic BFS ordering\",\n  \"directed\": false,\n  \"update_mode\": \"mixed\",\n  \"question\": \"can a lexicographic BFS (LexBFS) ordering be maintained under edge insertions and deletions? No efficient fully dynamic algorithm is known - this is an open problem.\"\n }\n]\n---\nusage: evoalgo init [-h] [--runs RUNS] [--run-id RUN_ID] [--goal GOAL]\n                    [--harness HARNESS]\n                    pack [dir]\n\npositional arguments:\n  pack               problem pack name, e.g. dynamic_bfs\n  dir                where the agent works (default: the run folder itself)\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help         show this help message and exit\n  --runs RUNS        run directory root (for the UI)\n  --run-id RUN_ID\n  --goal GOAL        research goal for this run\n  --harness HARNESS  which agent drives it (claude, codex, opencode), shown in\n                     the UI\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"evoalgo packs 2>&1; echo \"---\"; evoalgo init --help 2>&1","time":{"start":1792499810157,"end":1792499810194}},"id":"prt_159506e070012eaEtFWZm6H9Sj","sessionID":"ses_ea6b00f17ffeff7dL3uZ3RUV3t","messageID":"msg_1595061a800